    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 there's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes. The build also succeeds, confirming the OpenAPI generator produced the new `selfLink` field and MapStruct compiled the mapper without issue.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner id. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` string property (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits `getSelfLink()`/`setSelfLink()` on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` and a `selfLink(Owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null-safe when the id isn't assigned yet).\n\nDeriving it in the mapper means the field is populated consistently everywhere an `OwnerDto` is produced \u2014 both `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which the test exercises) and the `POST` create response \u2014 since the owner's id is already set in both paths. The `coreReturnsSelfLink` acceptance test passes, and the full suite reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
